A||||10||Jeff-87||87GT Idles but will not rev (dies when trying to accel)||||5||
Z||000000||Jeff-87||02-12-2001||12:17 AM||||Hi, This is my first post to this Forum.  I have been reading it for quite a while and would like to say thanks for all of the great information and help.<BR>My problem is that I can start the car, and it will idle.  When I give it some gas, it dies.  It is a 5 spd. 6cyl.  If have checked the following items.<BR>1.  Compression 120-130lbs (all cyl)<BR>2.  Check timing and appears to be correct.<BR>3.  Checked fuel pressure and it is between 40-45 (when I first turn the key, and when running)<BR>4.  Changed fuel filter.<BR>5.  No error codes from computer.<BR>6.  Changed spark plugs.  Look fine.  Front may be a little wet looking.<BR>7.  Fuses are all good.<P>I am wondering if anyone has ever had a timing chain jump a tooth?  Could this be the problem?  Also, Wondering a plugged cat. conv. would cause this problem?  I just purchased this car and it was in this condition when I bought it.  Any help would be greatly appreciated.<BR>Thanks,<BR>Jeff||||reg||5
Z||000001||ThatRickGuy||02-12-2001||09:17 AM||||usually if you jump a tooth the car will barily idle to begin with, may rev, but will stall when it has much of a load. It could be the timing advance, the metal weights in the bottom of the distributor, or someother part of the ignition system (coil, ign control mod) or it could be a clogged cat, when you hit the gas the preasure build causing a vapore lock.||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||02-12-2001||05:24 PM||||air filter clogged??? thatd do it<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 02-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||GT GT 87||02-12-2001||06:45 PM||||I now have an 87 GT , my last car,86 GT ,was not very fast. I had a 85 GT that was a rocket, and my 87 is fast. When I junked the 86 GT ( stripped), I tore down the engine and discover that the cam timing chain had an unreal amount of slack ,LIKE 1 1/4" left to right.It never skiped a tooth ,but I'm sure that is why it was so slow.(186,000 miles)            Steve||||reg||1
Z||000004||hugh||02-12-2001||07:36 PM||||It sounds like your cat.That will cause a pretty heavy restriction in the exhaust system.The quantity of exhaust gases at an idle are not very much,but when you step on the gas the exhaust volumne increases substantially and can't pass through the cat fast enough.I had them go bad on two of my vehicles over the years,and I could outrun them both for about 50 yards. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||02-12-2001||07:40 PM||||Do check the cat...<P>also<P>Check MAP sensor and all vacuum lines. MAP is used to calculate "vacuum advance." If MAP or it's line is messed up then the ECM will calc the wrong timing and you'll get this kind of problem.||||reg||1
Z||000006||ToddAsh||02-13-2001||07:57 PM||||I replaced th Cat on my daughters Jeep tonight.Wouldn't rev without stumbling,worse under load,hard to get above 45MPH. This happened overnight.Ran great last weekend when I drove it down the shore. Changed Cat back to normal or better. I'm taking mine off my Fiero.Todd||||reg||1
Z||000007||KnightRyder31||02-14-2001||06:30 PM||||I would check the cat.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Jeff-87||03-11-2001||11:21 PM||||Hi, just wanted to say thanks for the help.  I finally had time this weekend to work on it.  I notice that the egr tube was cracked and thought that might be it, but I sealed it with aluminum tape and it didn't change it.  Then, I unbolted the exhaust before that cat and it started up fine and rev's great.  Thanks for the help.<BR>Jeff||||reg||10
Z||000009||GoCartGuy||03-11-2001||11:28 PM||||Who needs the cat anyway....just added weight.<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT "The GoCart"||||reg||1
Z||000010||tgowens||03-12-2001||01:35 AM||||I would have suggested the cat too since there were no ECM codes.......remember, if you change your cat you should change your O2 sensor at the same time...........||||reg||1
